+## AGC 26.2 alpha13 - Topology-scale compute efficiency
+
+Alpha13 remodels the survival-scale layer around machine topology and duplicate-work removal for the target of ordinary survival servers with thousands of players at 20 TPS while preserving vanilla/Paper gameplay semantics and plugin compatibility.
+
+Added runtime components:
+
+- `AGCComputeTopologyPlanner` reserves CPU for the primary thread, plugins, Netty, GC and OS first, then allocates remaining compute only to semantic-safe helper lanes.
+- `AGCFanoutDeduplicator` turns repeated tick-local read-only fanout planning into shared plans without dropping packets or changing per-connection order.
+- `AGCChunkIntentPlanner` records FIFO chunk intent planning around existing Paper queues without reordering load/generate/send completion.
+- `AGCEntityVisibilityPreselector` prepares read-only tracker candidate sets without skipping entity tick, AI, damage or plugin events.
+- `AGCStorageIoGovernor` budgets IO/compression hints while leaving chunk status ownership and completion order unchanged.
+
+The important rule remains stricter than fallback-based optimisation: AGC may use more cores for read-only preparation and duplicate-work elimination, but Bukkit-visible mutation, plugin callbacks, redstone, entity ticking and chunk commit ordering stay in ordered lanes.
