+## R21 / alpha13 - Topology-scale compute efficiency
+
+Goal: make the thousand-player survival target less wasteful on real hardware without compromising gameplay or plugin semantics.
+
+Implemented in this slice:
+
+- CPU topology planner with primary-thread/plugin/Netty/GC reserve.
+- Tick-local fanout de-duplication for repeated read-only chunk/entity/cosmetic planning.
+- FIFO chunk intent planner that does not reorder Paper chunk queues.
+- Read-only entity visibility preselector with no entity tick/AI/interaction skipping.
+- Storage and compression helper governor for IO hints, not chunk ownership changes.
+- Public compute efficiency advice API and R21 E2E coverage.
+
+Next slices should wire these planners deeper into concrete hot paths after local JDK 25 Gradle validation: entity tracker candidate selection, chunk interest fanout, compression scheduling, and per-region survival hotspot measurements.
